### Local secrets / overrides — never commit these ###
*.env
.env.*
application-local.yaml
application-local.yml
application-local.properties

# ...except this one. The `local` profile is checked in deliberately: it is the profile
# `./mvnw spring-boot:run` activates, so a clean checkout that lacks it starts with a
# different security posture than the README describes. It holds no secrets — the local
# database credentials live in compose.yaml, which is committed for the same reason.
!src/main/resources/application-local.yaml

### Maven flatten plugin (build output, regenerated by every build) ###
.flattened-pom.xml
